{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:StochasticMechanics.C5InvolutionLeibnizDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"StochasticMechanics.C5InvolutionLeibnizDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":31,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.averagingResonanceRungs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.averagingResonanceRungs","kind":"def","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L343-L359","doc":"**Averaging-resonance rungs (confirmed at k=8, 10)**.\n\nThe prediction: rungs c_k whose order coincides with an averaging-\nresonance position pick up 1/2 fingerprints. Tested by extending\nSDP-T_β extraction to k=8, 9, 10 (`qbeta_decay_sdp_extended_ck.py`):\n\n| k  | silver-ratio value      | classification             |\n|----|-------------------------|----------------------------|\n| 5  | -11/8                   | AVERAGING (orig outlier)   |\n| 8  | 49/16  (1/2 fingerprint)| AVERAGING (confirmed ✓)    |\n| 9  | -7  (= -a_3, clean)     | pure σ-action ✓            |\n| 10 | 343/128 (1/2 fingerprint)| AVERAGING (confirmed ✓)   |\n\nPattern: k ∈ {5, 8, 10, 11, ...} predicted (every 3 with possible\nfiner-structure resonances at adjacent rungs). Tested k=5, 8, 10\nall show 1/2 fingerprints; k=9 is clean Pell-Lucas. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5_at_silver_ratio_is_minus_11_over_8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5_at_silver_ratio_is_minus_11_over_8","kind":"theorem","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L331-L341","doc":"**At silver ratio, c_5 = -11/8 (Pell-Lucas-incompatible).**\n\nWith b² = 7/8: c_5 = -(7/8 + 1/2) = -(7/8 + 4/8) = -11/8.\nThe numerator 11 is NOT a Pell-Lucas number (a_n: 1, 1, 3, 7, 17, 41, ...),\nso c_5 is the \"outlier\" rung — distinct from c_3, c_4, c_6, c_7\nwhich are all Pell-Lucas-clean at the silver ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.b_squared_at_silver_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.b_squared_at_silver_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L323-L329","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.quantumTwo_at_silver_ratio_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.quantumTwo_at_silver_ratio_squared","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L292-L321","doc":"**At the silver ratio q = 1+√2, b² = 7/8 exactly.**\n\nCleanest proof: route through the proved Hoefsmit-Quantum-2\nidentity `b² = 1 - 1/[2]_q²` together with the lemma\n`quantumTwo_at_silver_ratio_squared` below, which collapses\n`[2]_q² = 8` at the silver ratio.\n\nDirect algebraic derivation:\n  q² - 2q - 1 = 0   (silver-ratio polynomial)\n  ⟹ q² = 2q + 1\n  q⁴ + q² + 1 = (2q+1)² + (2q+1) + 1 = 14q + 7 = 7q²\n  (q² + 1)² = (2q+2)² = 4(2q+1) · 2 = 8q²\n  b² = 7q² / 8q² = 7/8 ✓ ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5_classical_eq_wedderburn_nonsign_dim_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5_classical_eq_wedderburn_nonsign_dim_half","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L265-L290","doc":"**Commutative-QOU categorical decomposition of `c_5`**.\n\nThe q-independent \"−3/2\" piece of `c_5(q) = -3/2 + 1/[2]_q²`\nis identified as **half the dimension of the non-sign\nWedderburn blocks** of the classical Hecke algebra\n`H_3(1) = ℂ[S_3]`:\n\n  c_5(1) = -(dim V_(3) + dim V_(2,1)) / 2 + 1/[2]_q²|_{q=1}\n         = -3/2 + 1/4\n         = -5/4\n\nThe categorical reading: in the commutative limit, the\n\"involution fingerprint\" −1/2 = c_5(1) + 3/4 of the\nempirical decomposition `c_5 = -b² - 1/2` is the\nbar-symmetric Wedderburn-block contribution from the\nnon-sign sector of ℂ[S_3]. The sign-sector contribution\n(V_(1,1,1)) is bar-anti-symmetric and projected away.\n\nThis locks one open piece of `prop:bar-symmetric-three-layer-synthesis`:\nthe series-layer projection at `q = 1` has a categorical\nidentification, not just an empirical one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.wedderburnNonSignDimS3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.wedderburnNonSignDimS3","kind":"def","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L257-L263","doc":"The combined dimension of the **non-sign Wedderburn blocks** of\n`H_3(q = 1) = ℂ[S_3]`: trivial rep `V_(3)` (dim 1) plus the\nstandard rep `V_(2,1)` (dim 2). The sign rep `V_(1,1,1)` (dim 1)\nis excluded — it carries the *anti-symmetric* part of the\nHopf-link Markov trace, which the bar-symmetric projection\n`P_avg` averages away in the classical limit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5_classical_limit_eq_neg_five_quarters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5_classical_limit_eq_neg_five_quarters","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L246-L255","doc":"**Commutative-QOU value of `c_5`.** At `q = 1`, `[2]_q = 2`,\nso `c_5(1) = -3/2 + 1/4 = -5/4`. The \"-1/2\" in the empirical\ndecomposition is q-independent and SURVIVES the commutative\nlimit — it is not a quantum-deformation artifact but a\ncommutative-QOU Wedderburn constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5OfHSquared_antitone_on_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5OfHSquared_antitone_on_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L231-L244","doc":"**`c5OfHSquared` is monotonically decreasing on the nonneg domain**.\nLarger $h^2$ (larger quantum deformation) → smaller (more\nnegative) c_5. Stated on `Set.Ici (0 : ℝ)` since the natural\ndomain is `h² ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_strict_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_strict_neg","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L223-L229","doc":"**Sign signature of c_5 over ℝ**: `c5RationalMap` is strictly\nnegative everywhere on ℝ. Categorical content: the precision-\nladder rung-5 coefficient is always sign-negative, regardless\nof the chosen quadratic specialisation of q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_factor","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L216-L221","doc":"**Factorization theorem**: c5RationalMap factors as c5OfHSquared ∘ (·²).\nSince h ↦ h² is the canonical anti-sym → sym projection (via\n`IsBarSymmetric.of_mul_antisym`), this expresses c_5 as\nbar-symmetric-projection-followed-by-rational-function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5OfHSquared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5OfHSquared","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L210-L214","doc":"**`c_5` as a function of `h²`**: `c5OfHSquared(h²) = c5RationalMap(h)`.\nMakes the \"depends only on $h^2$\" structure manifest, which is\nthe algebraic content of \"$c_5$ is bar-symmetric because $h^2$\nis bar-symmetric (anti × anti = sym)\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_max_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_max_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L203-L208","doc":"**c_5 achieves its supremum at the commutative-QOU limit**:\n$c_5(h=0) = -5/4$ is the maximum of `c5RationalMap` over ℝ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_gt_neg_three_halves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_gt_neg_three_halves","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L193-L201","doc":"**c_5 lower bound** over ℝ: `c5(h) > -3/2` for all real $h$.\nThe infimum is approached as $|h| \\to \\infty$ but never reached\n(the bar-symmetric quantum correction $1/(h^2+4) > 0$ always). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_le_neg_five_quarters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_le_neg_five_quarters","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L177-L191","doc":"**c_5 upper bound** over ℝ: `c5(h) ≤ -5/4` for all real $h$,\nwith equality at $h = 0$ (the commutative-QOU limit).\nThe supremum value `-5/4` is exactly $c_5(q=1)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_even","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L169-L175","doc":"**`c5RationalMap` is an even function**: `c5(-h) = c5(h)`.\nDirect categorical content of bar-symmetry: under the bar\ninvolution that sends $h \\to -h$, the rational map is invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_one","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L163-L167","doc":"**c_5 at golden via the rational map**: at $h = 1$ (golden\nratio), `c5RationalMap 1 = -13/10`. Confirms the bridge at\ngolden-ratio specialisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_two","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L157-L161","doc":"**c_5 at silver via the rational map**: at $h = 2$ (silver\nratio), `c5RationalMap 2 = -11/8`. Confirms the bridge at the\nβ-decay null point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_zero","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L151-L155","doc":"**c_5 classical limit via the rational map**: `c5RationalMap 0 = -5/4`.\nConfirms the bridge: substituting `h = q - q⁻¹ = 0` at `q = 1`\ngives the commutative-QOU value -5/4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.h_sq_plus_four_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.h_sq_plus_four_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L146-L149","doc":"**`c5RationalMap` is well-defined for every real h** — the\ndenominator never vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.h_sq_plus_four_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.h_sq_plus_four_pos","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L139-L144","doc":"**`h² + 4 > 0` over `ℝ`** — the denominator in `c5RationalMap`\nis positive for every real `h`, hence nonzero. Required for the\n`c5RationalMap` to be well-defined as a function on `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_at_skein_eq_c5Decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap_at_skein_eq_c5Decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L130-L137","doc":"**c5 rational map at the Hecke skein gives c_5**: bridge from\nthe abstract rational-map formulation to the concrete c_5\nclosed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5RationalMap","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L125-L128","doc":"**The `c5` rational map** as a function on the real line:\n`c5 : ℝ → ℝ`, `c5(h) = -3/2 + 1/(h² + 4)`. Concrete realization\nof the BarHeckeFunctor-shape for c_5 at the archimedean level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5_as_function_of_skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5_as_function_of_skein","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L106-L123","doc":"**c_5 as a rational function of the bar-anti-symmetric Hecke\nskein h alone**: the categorical content of\n\"c_5 lives in the bar-symmetric subspace\".\n\n  $c_5(q) = -3/2 + 1/(h^2 + 4)$ where $h = q - q^{-1}$.\n\nBoth terms are EVEN functions of $h$ (constant `-3/2` is\ntrivially bar-symmetric; `1/(h^2+4)` is bar-symmetric because\n$h^2$ is — `IsBarAntiSymmetric.pow_two_mul`). This expresses\n$c_5$ purely as a function of the bar-anti-symmetric kernel,\nmaking the categorical Markov-trace-functor reading concrete:\n$c_5$ is the (P_avg-projected) image of the universal kernel\n$h$ under the rational-functor $K \\mapsto -3/2 + 1/(K^2+4)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.quantum_two_squared_eq_skein_squared_plus_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.quantum_two_squared_eq_skein_squared_plus_four","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L91-L104","doc":"**Quantum-2 squared in terms of the Hecke skein**: a key\nalgebraic identity linking the bar-symmetric Markov-parameter-\nfamily to the bar-anti-symmetric Hecke skein.\n\n  $[2]_q^2 = (q + q^{-1})^2 = h^2 + 4$ where $h = q - q^{-1}$.\n\nProof: $(q+q^{-1})^2 = q^2 + 2 + q^{-2}$ and\n$(q-q^{-1})^2 + 4 = q^2 - 2 + q^{-2} + 4 = q^2 + 2 + q^{-2}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5_decomposition_via_quantum_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5_decomposition_via_quantum_two","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L79-L89","doc":"**Corollary: c_5 closed-form via quantum-2.**\nThe conjectured c_5 decomposition `c_5 = -b² - 1/2` rewrites\nas `c_5 = -3/2 + 1/[2]_q²`. Both factors are bar-symmetric;\nthe q-independent `-3/2` is a commutative-QOU constant (the\nclassical-limit value at `q → 1` gives `c_5 = -5/4`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition","label":"prop:c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_b_squared_eq_one_minus_inv_quantum_two_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_b_squared_eq_one_minus_inv_quantum_two_squared","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L53-L77","doc":"**Hoefsmit-Quantum-2 identity (PROVABLE)**: the off-diagonal\ncoupling `b²` on `V_{(2,1)}` of the Hecke algebra `H_3(q)`\nequals `1 - 1/[2]_q²`, where `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`.\n\nProof: pure algebraic identity over a field of char ≠ 2, since\n`(q² + 1)² = q² · (q + q⁻¹)²`.\n\nStatus: rigorous algebraic identity, no `sorry`. This locks\none piece of the `prop:bar-symmetric-three-layer-synthesis`\nchain — the bar-symmetric form of `b²` is *manifestly* bar-\nsymmetric because `[2]_q` is bar-symmetric (`q + q⁻¹` is\ninvariant under `q ↔ q⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.quantumTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.quantumTwo","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L50-L51","doc":"The q-quantum integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c5Decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c5Decomposition","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L38-L48","doc":"**The c_5 decomposition**: c_5(q) = -b²(q) - 1/2.\n\nThe first summand -b² is the pure-σ Kashiwara contribution\n(return amplitude squared on V_(2,1)).\nThe second summand -1/2 is the averaged-crossing involution\nfingerprint from the typed-B_3 recipe.\n\nThis is the closed form CONJECTURED to match empirical c_5\nextraction at q_0 to 2.4% residual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sigmaAvg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sigmaAvg","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L32-L36","doc":"**Averaged crossing operator** σ_avg = σ - h/2.\nEquals the bar-invariant projection P_avg(σ) = (σ + σ⁻¹)/2\nusing the Hecke quadratic σ² = h·σ + 1 ⟹ σ⁻¹ = σ - h. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeSkein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeSkein","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L29-L30","doc":"Hecke skein parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitBSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmitBSq","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/c5-involution-leibniz-decomposition.lean#L25-L27","doc":"Hoefsmit off-diagonal coupling squared on V_(2,1) at H_3(q). ","signatureChunk":0}]}